  "label": "Emotional Appeal in Charity",
  "description": "Charity campaigns often use emotional appeals to motivate donations by evoking feelings of compassion, guilt, or responsibility. The image of an adult hand holding a child’s hand is a classic visual trope used to trigger empathy. The text 'for just ten cents a day' is designed to make the donation seem small and accessible, leveraging the psychological principle of low-barrier giving.",
